utation test (sanity: is the test discriminating?) | 1,602 diff lines → yes |\n\nAll 16 exports covered: `stbds_arrgrowf`, `stbds_arrfreef`, `stbds_rand_seed`, `stbds_hash_string`, `stbds_hash_bytes`, `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts`, `stbds_hmput_default`, `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_hmfree_func`, `stbds_shmode_func`, `stbds_stralloc`, `stbds_strreset`, `strkey`, `arr_del`.\n\n## C quirks deliberately preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n1. **SipHash sign-extension bug** — `data = d[0] | (d[1]<<8) | (d[2]<<16) | (d[3]<<24)` is an `int` in C; when `d[3] >= 0x80` it goes negative and sign-extends on assignment to `size_t`, flooding the upper 32 bits with ones. Reproduced as `(lo as i32) as usize`. My mutation test confirms this changes 1,602 output lines — it genuinely matters.\n2. Same issue in the tail `switch` at `case 4: data |= (d[3] << 24)`.\n3. **Missing `temp_key` store** in the *second* probe loop of `stbds_hmput_key` (the first loop sets it, the wrap-around loop doesn't) — kept asymmetric.\n4. `hash ^= hash ^ ROTR(hash,n)` self-cancelling XORs in `stbds_hash_string` — transcribed literally.\n5. `stbds_arrgrowf(NULL, n, 0, 0)` returns `NULL` (so `stbds_header()` on it faults) — preserved; this is what made my first harness segfault *identically* in both libraries.\n6. `STBDS_ASSERT` is compiled out under `NDEBUG` in the C release build, so asserts are no-ops in Rust rather than panics — this avoids introducing aborts the C `.so` doesn't have.\n\nImplementation notes: `#[repr(C)]` structs mirror the C layouts exactly (including the 64-byte-aligned bucket storage carved out of one `realloc`), and the crate calls libc `realloc`/`free`/`mem*`/`str*` directly so memory is interchangeable with the C library's. Arithmetic uses explicit `wrapping_*` throughout to match C's unsigned wraparound. `sprintf(buffer, \"test_%d\", n)` is reimplemented digit-by-digit (correct for `INT_MIN`) writing into the same 256-byte static.\n\nI removed my scratch build/test directories; `c_src/` is unmodified and the deliverable is just `translation/Cargo.toml` + `translation/src/lib.rs` (1,315 lines).","ttft_ms":2820,"ttft_stream_ms":2653,"time_to_request_ms":59,"type":"result","duration_ms":701310,"uuid":"9ab39863-49d0-4b36-ba25-cfafdd6f0284","queued_turn_count":0}
